{"from": "passage:mk-04-12", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-13-14", "note": "Mark frames the Isaiah 6:9-10 quotation as purpose ('lest they should turn again, and their sins should be forgiven them'); Matthew 13:14-15 applies it with the 'healing' clause of Isaiah 6:10b."}
{"from": "passage:mk-04-21", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-05-15", "note": "Mark adds 'or under a bed' to the lamp saying; Matthew has basket and stand only."}
{"from": "passage:mk-04-24", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-07-02", "note": "The same measure-for-measure saying stands in the Sermon on the Mount at Matthew 7:2."}
{"from": "passage:mk-04-25", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-13-12"}
{"from": "passage:mk-04-31", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-13-31", "note": "Matthew has the seed sown 'in his field'; Mark says sown 'in the earth'."}
