{"from": "claim:mk-04-11-12-mystery-isaiah-6", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-13-14-15-isaiah-6-quoted", "note": "Both quote Isaiah 6:9-10; Mark frames it as purpose ('lest they should turn again, and their sins should be forgiven them') where Matthew adds the 'healing' clause of Isaiah 6:10b and cites it as fulfilled."}
{"from": "claim:mk-04-11-12-mystery-isaiah-6", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:isaiah-6-9-10", "note": "The quoted source text (biblical cross-reference, not external evidence)."}
{"from": "artifact:great-isaiah-scroll", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-04-11-12-mystery-isaiah-6", "grade": "B", "note": "The Great Isaiah Scroll (ca. 125 BCE) preserves Isaiah 6:9-10, the text quoted; it attests the quoted wording behind the citation, not that Jesus applied it to his hearers (reused from ch 13)."}
{"from": "observation:cereal-growth-stages-bbch", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-cereal-growth-scales"}
{"from": "observation:cereal-growth-stages-bbch", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-04-26-29-seed-grows-secretly", "grade": "C", "note": "Modern agronomy stages cereal growth from leaf development through inflorescence emergence (heading, the ear) to ripe grain - the sequence 'first the blade, then the ear, then the full grain in the ear' is real cereal phenology. Modern observation, not a first-century witness."}
{"from": "artifact:galilee-boat", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-04-36-other-boats", "grade": "C", "note": "A 1st-century fishing boat from the lake: small boats crowded the Sea of Galilee. Context for 'other small boats', not the event."}
{"from": "artifact:galilee-boat", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mk-04-38-asleep-in-stern", "grade": "C", "note": "The excavated boat is 8.2 m long and 2.3 m wide - room at the stern to lie down out of the rowers' way. It shows the setting, not the cushion, for which no fetched evidence exists."}
